      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining NoSQL Provider**\n\nI'm zeroing in on AWS DynamoDB as the managed NoSQL provider for the `fetch_document.py` script. The goal is to make this external provider identifiable within the Python file, establishing a clear link to the service the code will interact with.\n\n\n**Pinpointing DynamoDB Integration**\n\nMy thought process has solidified around DynamoDB. I'm moving beyond just identifying it; I'm strategizing the `fetch_document.py` implementation. I'm focusing now on establishing a function to retrieve documents, using `boto3` to interface with the DynamoDB client and defining the parameters, `table_name` and `document_id`, for document retrieval.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789860742514,
          "start": 1789860740873
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc037f09001Uql38vpBgqtU7V",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc037a00001XJ2TkKV7oaWEqM",
      "session_id": "ses_f43fc8611ffeW3T8PODo0tykav",
